    <bpmn:process id="W_W4129" name="W4129. Inventory Strategy, Postponement &amp; Pooling Policy" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Strategy refresh; category review; network change
Frequency: Annual + per category
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs across 4 DCs + 200 stores
Owner: Network Strategy Lead / Merchandising (VS-01)
Participants: Merchandising (VS-01), Supply Planning (VS-02), Finance (VS-17.4/VS-105)
Source: workflow W4129 — Inventory Strategy, Postponement &amp; Pooling Policy</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4129_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4129_Lane1" name="Network Strategy Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4129_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4129_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4129_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4129_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4129_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4129_Start3" name="Strategy refresh; category review; network change">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4129_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4129_Task4" name="Network Strategy/Merchandising define the inventory strategy per category…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Network Strategy/Merchandising define the inventory strategy per category: where to stock (DC vs store vs both), postponement (e.g., paint tinting at store links to VS-09), pooling, and make-to-stock vs make-to-order
Responsible (R): Network Strategy Lead / Merchandising / Supply Planning
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4129_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4129_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4129_Task5" name="Network Strategy set the inventory positioning policy (centralized vs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Network Strategy set the inventory positioning policy (centralized vs decentralized, forward-stocking, cross-dock for fast-movers links to VS-04) aligned to network design (W4121)
Responsible (R): Network Strategy Lead
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4129_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4129_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4129_Task6" name="Network Strategy document the strategy, align with merchandising/finance on the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Network Strategy document the strategy, align with merchandising/finance on the turn/service trade-off, and feed into MEIO (W4130) and parameter governance (W4135)
Responsible (R): Network Strategy Lead / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain / COO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4129_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4129_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4129_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4129_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4129_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-639 (ensure controlled execution — Multi-Echelon Inventory Optimization &amp; Service-Level Engineering (PA-136.2).) | - CTL-639: inventory strategy approved by Merchandising/Supply Chain/Finance
Owner: Network Strategy Lead / Merchandising (VS-01)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4129_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4129_Annotation8" targetRef="W4129_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
