    <bpmn:process id="W_W4130" name="W4130. Multi-Echelon Inventory Optimization (MEIO) Modeling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Network/inventory decision; parameter refresh
Frequency: Continuous + periodic refresh
Volume: ~7.2M parameter sets (per SKU per location); 35K SKUs × 205 locations
Owner: Network Strategy Lead / Supply Chain Analytics (VS-28)
Participants: Analytics (VS-28), Supply Planning (VS-02), Merchandising (VS-01)
Source: workflow W4130 — Multi-Echelon Inventory Optimization (MEIO) Modeling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4130_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4130_Lane1" name="Network Strategy Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4130_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4130_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4130_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4130_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4130_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4130_Start3" name="Network/inventory decision; parameter refresh">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4130_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4130_Task4" name="Network Strategy/Analytics build and maintain the MEIO model: demand…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Network Strategy/Analytics build and maintain the MEIO model: demand variability and lead-time variability per SKU per echelon, dependency between echelons (DC buffers protect stores), and the service-level target per segment (W4132)
Responsible (R): Network Strategy Lead / Analytics
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4130_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4130_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4130_Task5" name="Network Strategy/Analytics run MEIO optimization to find the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Network Strategy/Analytics run MEIO optimization to find the least-inventory-cost deployment that meets service targets across all echelons (vs siloed per-location safety stock), and quantify working-capital/service impact
Responsible (R): Network Strategy Lead / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per refresh</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4130_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4130_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4130_Task6" name="Network Strategy output optimized parameters (safety stock, ROP, EOQ, min/max)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Network Strategy output optimized parameters (safety stock, ROP, EOQ, min/max) to MDM (W4135) for execution by supply planning (VS-02), and validate post-implementation (W4138)
Responsible (R): Network Strategy Lead / Supply Planning
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Per refresh</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4130_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4130_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4130_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4130_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4130_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-639 (ensure controlled execution — Multi-Echelon Inventory Optimization &amp; Service-Level Engineering (PA-136.2).) | - CTL-639: MEIO assumptions documented; parameters governed before publishing
Owner: Network Strategy Lead / Supply Chain Analytics (VS-28)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
